            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_cmd_helper.cpp",
                    "line": 35,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tom Joseph",
                        "email": "rushtotom@gmail.com",
                        "username": "tomjoseph83"
                    },
                    "message": "This is spec specific range, so instead of single map we need to split this into type specific and generic completion codes."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_cmd_helper.cpp",
                    "line": 35,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rajeev Ranjan",
                        "email": "ranjan.rajeev1609@gmail.com",
                        "username": "rajeeranjan"
                    },
                    "message": "Having all error codes consolidated in a single map simplifies updating completion codes. Given that the error code enums are unique, do you see additional value in splitting them?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_cmd_helper.cpp",
                    "line": 35,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Is this going to be a multi-map? Else. the keys will collide across types."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_cmd_helper.cpp",
                    "line": 35,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tom Joseph",
                        "email": "rushtotom@gmail.com",
                        "username": "tomjoseph83"
                    },
                    "message": "There are overlapping completion codes based on type. \nDSP0248 aka T2 - INVALID_SENSOR_ID = 0x80\nDSP0267 aka T5 - NOT_IN_UPDATE_MODE = 0x80"
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_cmd_helper.cpp",
                    "line": 35,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rajeev Ranjan",
                        "email": "ranjan.rajeev1609@gmail.com",
                        "username": "rajeeranjan"
                    },
                    "message": "Updated the code to handle overlapping completion codes depending on the PLDM type.\n\nWill extend it for T2 as part of T2 command integration. One thing to note is in T2, completion codes can also overlap depending on the command.\n\ne.g PLDM_PLATFORM_INVALID_EFFECTER_ID = 0x80,\nPLDM_PLATFORM_INVALID_SENSOR_ID = 0x80,\nPLDM_PLATFORM_INVALID_DATA_TRANSFER_HANDLE = 0x80,\nPLDM_PLATFORM_INVALID_PROTOCOL_TYPE = 0x80,"
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_cmd_helper.cpp",
                    "line": 59,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tom Joseph",
                        "email": "rushtotom@gmail.com",
                        "username": "tomjoseph83"
                    },
                    "message": "Updating the existing commands to use fillCompletionCode is in the scope of this commit or a followup commit?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_cmd_helper.cpp",
                    "line": 59,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rajeev Ranjan",
                        "email": "ranjan.rajeev1609@gmail.com",
                        "username": "rajeeranjan"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes that will be a follow-up commit."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_cmd_helper.cpp",
                    "line": 59,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                        "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manojkiraneda"
                    },
                    "message": "Would that be for all the commands that pldmtool implement ? or only for FW update commands ? Would be great if you can integrate this with all the commands."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_cmd_helper.cpp",
                    "line": 59,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rajeev Ranjan",
                        "email": "ranjan.rajeev1609@gmail.com",
                        "username": "rajeeranjan"
                    },
                    "message": "Yeah, I'll make changes for all the commands in the follow-up patches"
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_cmd_helper.cpp",
                    "line": 68,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Can you add testing details?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_cmd_helper.cpp",
                    "line": 68,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rajeev Ranjan",
                        "email": "ranjan.rajeev1609@gmail.com",
                        "username": "rajeeranjan"
                    },
                    "message": "Only added helper utility in this patch, test results for each command would be attached in the subsequent patches, e.g. https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/pldm/+/79167/3?usp=related-change"
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_cmd_helper.hpp",
                    "line": 64,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tom Joseph",
                        "email": "rushtotom@gmail.com",
                        "username": "tomjoseph83"
                    },
                    "message": "Does this cover both PLDM T0 & PLDM T5 completion codes?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_cmd_helper.hpp",
                    "line": 64,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rajeev Ranjan",
                        "email": "ranjan.rajeev1609@gmail.com",
                        "username": "rajeeranjan"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes it will"
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_cmd_helper.hpp",
                    "line": 68,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Do we also show the numeric RC?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_cmd_helper.hpp",
                    "line": 68,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rajeev Ranjan",
                        "email": "ranjan.rajeev1609@gmail.com",
                        "username": "rajeeranjan"
                    },
                    "message": "Using the verbose flag, we can always get the raw command response.\n\nFor example -\n\npldmtool fw_update RequestUpdate --max_transfer_size 32 --num_comps 2 --max_transfer_reqs 10 --package_data_length 10 --comp_img_ver_str_type ASCII --comp_img_ver_str_len 4 --comp_img_set_ver_str ver1 -m 0 -v\npldmtool: <6> Tx: 00 01 80 05 10 20 00 00 00 02 00 0a 0a 00 01 04 76 65 72 31\nSuccess in creating the socket : RC = 5\nSuccess in connecting to socket : RC = 0\nSuccess in sending message type as pldm to mctp demux daemon : RC = 1\npldmtool: <6> Rx: 00 05 10 00 00 00 00\n{\n    \"CompletionCode\": \"SUCCESS\",\n    \"FirmwareDeviceMetaDataLength\": 0,\n    \"FDWillSendGetPackageDataCommend\": \"0x00\"\n}"
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_cmd_helper.hpp",
                    "line": 68,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rajeev Ranjan",
                        "email": "ranjan.rajeev1609@gmail.com",
                        "username": "rajeeranjan"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
